@@ -0,0 +1,55 @@
+# Visitor SMS (Talksasa) — setup and change notes
+
+## What changed
+
+1. **Auto-selected department.** When a visit is booked (web form or mobile API) without a
+   host staff member *or* a department, the department of the person booking is used.
+   If that person has no department, the form asks them to choose one.
+2. **SMS to the host only.** Visitor notifications are sent only by SMS (Talksasa BulkSMS)
+   and only to the host. Email, in-app and WhatsApp messages for visitor events were removed.
+   The host is:
+   - the selected host staff member, otherwise
+   - the HOD of the selected (or auto-selected) department, otherwise
+   - the person who booked the visit.
+
+   SMS are sent when a visit is booked, when the visitor is checked in at the gate,
+   when a visit is cancelled (unless the host cancelled it), and to the new host if
+   the host is changed while the visit is still scheduled.
+3. **Host mobile number, saved until changed.** The booking form shows who will get the SMS
+   and pre-fills their saved mobile number. If none is saved, the number is required. Whatever
+   is entered is saved to the host's user profile and reused on later bookings until someone
+   changes it. Every user can also save their own number on the Visitor Dashboard.
+   Numbers are stored as +2547XXXXXXXX / +2541XXXXXXXX.
+4. **System → SMS Settings** (administrators): enable/disable, API endpoint, API token,
+   sender ID, and a "Send test SMS" button. The WhatsApp Config menu item was removed.
+5. Each SMS result (sent / failed and why) is written to the appointment's Activity Log and
+   shown on screen.
+
+No database migration is needed and no new Python package is required
+(the Talksasa client uses only the standard library).
+
+## Setup
+
+1. Deploy the files and restart the application.
+2. Sign in as an administrator → **System → SMS Settings** (`/Operations/system/sms/`).
+3. Paste the Talksasa **API token**, enter your approved **Sender ID**, keep the endpoint
+   `https://bulksms.talksasa.com/api/v3/`, set **Enable SMS Notifications** to Enabled, save.
+4. Use **Send Test SMS** with your own number.
+
+Alternatively set `TALKSASA_API_TOKEN`, `TALKSASA_SENDER_ID` and `TALKSASA_API_URL` in `.env`;
+values saved on the SMS Settings page take priority.
+
+## Talksasa request used
+
+    POST https://bulksms.talksasa.com/api/v3/sms/send
+    Authorization: Bearer <API token>
+    Content-Type: application/json
+    {"recipient": "254712345678", "sender_id": "<sender id>", "type": "plain", "message": "..."}
+
+## Files
+
+New:      apps/visitors/sms.py, templates/settings_manager/sms.html, SMS_SETUP.md
+Changed:  apps/visitors/{models,forms,views,notifications,urls}.py, apps/visitors/api/views.py,
+          apps/settings_manager/{models,views,urls}.py, templates/base.html,
+          templates/visitors/{form,detail,dashboard}.html
+Unused (kept, not linked): apps/visitors/whatsapp.py and the WhatsApp config page/model.
